1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:02,640
Data is no longer just information.

2
00:00:02,730 --> 00:00:04,410
It is exposure.

3
00:00:05,070 --> 00:00:14,100
For today's businesses, a single inspection can expose years of
scattered records, weak controls and unanswered compliance risks.

4
00:00:14,430 --> 00:00:16,540
Picture a publicly listed company.

5
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:23,460
Thousands of customer records spread across departments,
buried in systems, files and everyday processes.

6
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:25,980
Valuable, yet unprotected.

7
00:00:26,310 --> 00:00:29,670
This is where the 90-day
inspection-ready plan begins.

8
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:31,240
Phase one, diagnose.

9
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:34,920
In just 20 days, hidden gaps
are brought into the light.

10
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:36,430
Phase two, build.

11
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:45,600
From days 21 to 60, policies, logs and accountability are
put firmly in place, led by a named data protection officer.

12
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:47,860
Phase three, operationalise.

13
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:50,400
Compliance moves from paper to practice.

14
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:56,190
Teams are trained, controls are lived, and a
breach simulation proves the response holds.

15
00:00:56,310 --> 00:00:59,310
By day 90, the business
is inspection ready.

16
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:02,700
Defensible, structured and built to last.

17
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:03,850
No delays.

18
00:01:03,930 --> 00:01:05,160
No surprises.

19
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:06,480
Just clarity.

20
00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:09,420
And that exposed, chaotic web of data?

21
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:13,100
It becomes controlled,
organised, protected.
